            "historyPhysical": "<strong>Chief Complaint:</strong> Worsening hypotension and altered mental status on Post-Op Day 2.<br/><strong>HPI:</strong> Client underwent emergency exploratory laparotomy for a perforated bowel 48 hours ago. Initial recovery was stable, but over the last 6 hours, the client has developed increasing tachycardia and a decrease in mean arterial pressure (MAP). Fluid resuscitation was initiated on the ward, but the client was transferred to the ICU for vasopressor support.<br/><strong>PMH:</strong> Hypertension, Type 2 Diabetes, COPD (Gold Stage II).<br/><strong>Physical Exam:</strong> Client is lethargic but arousable to verbal stimuli. Skin is warm and flushed in the core but peripherally cool. Abdomen is distended and tender with hypoactive bowel sounds. Surgical incision is intact with serosanguinous drainage.",
